Thank you for the kind words and the thoughtful questions — happy to address each one.

1. Source of Playbooks
The playbooks were built by combining technical guidance sourced from Confluence with coverage for new and emerging technologies identified by our team. Each playbook was crafted to address real-world Codemind use cases across development, testing, security, and architecture domains.

2. Testing & Validation Status
We have tested and validated several playbooks to date, including:
- Developer and testing workflow playbooks
- TOGAF Risk Matrix
- Functional Inventory Analyzer
- Security Review
- Component Taxonomy
- Component SBOM Generation

Not all playbooks have been tested yet — our approach is pragmatic: we test and enhance each playbook when an actual use case or requirement arises, ensuring improvements are driven by real feedback rather than hypothetical scenarios.

3. Enterprise Standard Storage
For enterprise-standard playbooks, we follow the established Prompt L as the canonical store. Playbooks such as Testing, BlackDuck, and Checkmarx are already published there. The remaining playbooks are available via Git, where developers can download and use them directly — they are ready to use as-is.

We will continue to expand coverage, validate more playbooks, and migrate mature ones to the Prompt Library progressively. Thank you for looping in Manish — we welcome any contributions or feedback from the broader team.

